reated_at":"2024-04-30T23:03:29Z","performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/2139339258","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/11332#issuecomment-2139339258","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/11332","id":2139339258,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCX5JB85_g7n6","user":{"login":"rubinghv","id":10511617,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTExNjE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10511617?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubinghv","html_url":"https://github.com/rubinghv","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubinghv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubinghv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubinghv/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubinghv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubinghv/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubinghv/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubinghv/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubinghv/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubinghv/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-05-30T11:21:36Z","updated_at":"2024-05-30T11:22:05Z","body":"I recently had a regression where `bulk_save_objects()` was no longer able to handle adding two linked ORM objects. I.e. College object which has a relationship with Students. Previously when I added a bunch of College objects, each of which contained the students parameter which was a list of Student objects, no issues occurred and it added both successfully to respective tables linked by a foreign key. Now with nothing changing on my end, it only adds the College(s) and produces no error. I checked and changing nothing, it does work correctly with `session.add()`. \r\n\r\nIs there any chance that co